{
  "reason": "s91. The page (UGLAS/BIO_BA_BS/BIO_BA/, cached 2026-07-25, read 2026-09-23) prints 'Biology BA Major Electives: See approved list in tab above ... Approved Biology BA electives courses 15, Take 4 additional credits from either Biology Distribution Electives or Approved Biology BA Electives 4'. The tab's list is scraped as 'requirements' and becomes that row's pool at build time (build_data _TAB_LIST_POOLS). A distribution course and an elective are one exclusive set: a course pays one of the two rows (the UF Online page states it: 'Cannot be counted as both an elective and a Biology Distribution Course'). [Ported from UF Planner, whose reviewer checked the 2025-2026 page. 2026-10-12: this parse of the 2026-2027 page lists exactly the requirement courses that reviewer accepted, so the review carries over.] [2026-10-18, https://catalog.ufl.edu/UGRD/colleges-schools/UGLAS/BIO_BA_BS/BIO_BA/: 'Biology Distribution Courses' prints 'Complete one course or course/lab combination from 3 of the 5 Groups. 9' over Groups 1-5, but parsed as a 'take all' list of 39 rows for 9 credits. Now a 9-credit, three-course chooser whose options are the ten three-group combinations (so the courses come from three groups; one from EACH is not enforced, and 'Only one 2000-level course may be applied' is left to the advisor). The exclusive set is kept.] [2026-10-18, https://catalog.ufl.edu/UGRD/colleges-schools/UGLAS/BIO_BA_BS/BIO_BA/: the reason above relies on UF Planner's build step (_TAB_LIST_POOLS), which this repo does not have, so the 'Take 4 additional credits' row (an empty 4-credit list) is now a 4-credit chooser over the distribution courses and the approved BA electives.]",
